# digits16 - the clock face.
#
# 10x16 with 2px stems, which is about the largest that still fits HH:MM across
# a 64px column: 4 digits at 10px, a 4px colon, and four 2px gaps comes to 52px.
#
# Codepoints 45-58 only: - . / then 0-9 then the colon. The range has to stay
# contiguous for glyph indexing. Anything outside it is skipped when drawn in
# this font, so use tom5x7 for labels.
#
# The hyphen earns its place: the clock renders "--:--" before the first SNTP
# sync, and without a '-' glyph that placeholder collapses to a bare colon.

@name     digits16
@role     digits
@height   16
@baseline 16
@gap      2

